prompt.text:
Repair the CommonJS module below. It is intended to export exactly `{ chooseAsset }`.

`chooseAsset(primary, alternatives)` must accept a `primary` string and an array of alternative strings. Normalize every string by trimming it. Empty strings are unusable. Return the first usable value, considering the primary first and then alternatives in their original order. Repeated values are allowed and have no special effect. Return `null` if none is usable. Non-string primary values, non-array alternatives, or non-string alternative elements must throw `TypeError`. Do not mutate the alternatives array.

The current implementation incorrectly gives alternatives priority over a usable primary. Return a corrected complete source file.

```javascript
'use strict';

function chooseAsset(primary, alternatives) {
  if (typeof primary !== 'string' || !Array.isArray(alternatives)) {
    throw new TypeError('invalid input');
  }
  const normalized = alternatives.map((value) => {
    if (typeof value !== 'string') throw new TypeError('invalid alternative');
    return value.trim();
  });
  normalized.push(primary.trim());
  for (const value of normalized) {
    if (value !== '') return value;
  }
  return null;
}

module.exports = { chooseAsset };
```

